From fca9e7e25d6aa2af5891c7a86efeecbca088d6f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stel777 <274792865+Stel777@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 16 Jun 2026 20:08:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 09/11] feat(source-folders): share /update-brain's vault
 layout so they reconcile
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The in-app Sync now mirrors into `_source_files/<folder name>/<relpath>` —
the exact layout the /update-brain skill writes — instead of its own
`<slug-hash>/` path. Because the same source file now lands at the same
vault path under both tools, they reconcile against each other instead of
duplicating: either tool can import a folder and the other recognizes its
files (matching engrams.filename → ingest's hash check skips the re-import).

- source_slug (sanitized + blake3 hash) → source_subdir (raw folder name,
  matching the skill's `source.name`).
- vault_rel_for now yields `_source_files/<name>/<rel>`.
- mirror_one_file adopts a file already present at its path (e.g. imported
  by the skill) into the manifest without re-copying.
- plan() classifies already-present files as `unchanged`, so the preview is
  honest about what the skill already put in the brain.
- The skill itself is unchanged.

Verified on a throwaway brain: Sync writes the _source_files layout; after
wiping Sync's manifest (simulating an independent skill import) a re-sync
kept the count flat (no duplication) and the preview correctly showed the
files as unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
